  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe attributes described in [this section of the spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#client-identification) are heavily \"muted,\" largely for privacy reasons.\n\nFor example, `navigator.platform` is explicitly permitted to lie and return the value for another platform.\n\nAnd there is this tracking-vector warning covering the whole section (emphasis mine):\n\n> Any information in this API that varies from user to user can be used to profile the user. In fact, if enough such information is available, a user can actually be uniquely identified. **For this reason, user agent implementers are strongly urged to include as little information in this API as possible.**\n\nOver in https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27342, there's a dispute over whether all of this constitutes a \"deprecation.\" By that, I basically mean: is it WHATWG's opinion that web developers should avoid these APIs?\n\n",
